<think> Okay, so here's this problem about two identical cylindrical vessels connected at the bottom with a small-diameter tube that has a valve. When the valve was closed, water was poured into the first vessel and oil was poured into the second vessel such that the liquid levels were identical and equal to h = 40 cm. Now, we need to figure out at what level the water will establish itself in the first vessel once the valve is opened. They also give us the densities of the two liquids: density of water is 1000 kg/m³ and density of oil is 700 kg/m³. We are told to neglect the volume of the connecting tube. The answer should be in centimeters, inside a box.

